## DC 3 — System Components

### 3.1 Infrastructure

| Layer | Component |
|---|---|
| Cloud provider | Microsoft Azure |
| Operating system | Linux (managed services) |
| Container orchestration | Azure Kubernetes Service (`aks-normain-prod-01`) with Istio service mesh providing mTLS between workloads |
| Container registry | Azure Container Registry (shared `acrnormain` plus per-environment `acrnormainprod01`) |
| Primary database | Azure Database for PostgreSQL — Flexible Server (version 16, network-private) |
| Object storage | Azure Blob Storage (per-tenant containers) |
| Shared file storage | Azure Files — Premium FileStorage, NFS protocol, per-tenant share |
| Email delivery | Azure Communication Services (`acs-email-normain-prod-01`) |
| AI compute | Azure OpenAI Service (multiple EU regions — see 3.5) and Azure Document Intelligence (Sweden Central) |
| Observability | Azure Log Analytics workspace (`law-normain-audit-prod-01`, 365-day retention) plus Azure Storage immutable tier for audit logs |
| Secret management | Azure Key Vault (RBAC-authorised, soft-delete plus purge-protection enabled). Stores application secrets and OAuth credentials; encryption at rest of customer data uses Microsoft-managed keys, not Key Vault customer-managed keys. |
| Edge / DNS | Cloudflare (authoritative DNS for `normain.com`) |

### 3.2 Software

| Tier | Components |
|---|---|
| Application | Normain platform web UI, per-tenant API service (`api`), per-tenant background worker (`worker`), and platform Tenant API (`tenant-api`) which fronts Microsoft Marketplace subscription lifecycle and triggers tenant provisioning |
| Data plane | Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server (per-tenant database within a shared server), Azure Blob Storage (per-tenant container), Azure Files NFS (per-tenant share), per-tenant Redis (in-cluster) |
| Customer input integrations | SharePoint, Google Drive, Box (read-only via OAuth), plus direct UI upload and customer-supplied URL ingestion (web content via Firecrawl) |

### 3.3 People

Functions: Engineering, Product, Customer Operations, Go-to-Market, Finance & Legal. ISMS roles assigned per the ISMS Roles & Responsibilities document. The Chief Technology Officer is designated as the Information Security Management Leader and the Data Protection Officer.

### 3.4 Data

| Data state | Protection |
|---|---|
| In transit (customer ↔ platform) | TLS 1.2 or higher. HTTPS is terminated at the Istio Gateway with per-tenant certificates issued via cert-manager and Let's Encrypt; HTTP is redirected to HTTPS at the route level. |
| In transit (platform ↔ external subprocessor) | TLS 1.2 or higher. |
| In transit (within the Azure VNet) | mTLS between pods via the Istio service mesh. The NFS share between worker pods and Azure Files runs unencrypted within the customer-isolated VNet, restricted by VNet network rules to API and AKS subnets. |
| At rest (database, blob, NFS, audit log storage, backups) | AES-256, Azure platform-managed encryption with Microsoft-managed keys. |
| Application-layer encryption | Selected sensitive fields are additionally encrypted with an application-managed key stored in Azure Key Vault. |
| Application secrets | Stored in Azure Key Vault and mounted to workload pods via the Secrets Store CSI Driver and Azure Workload Identity (no long-lived secrets are stored in pods for Azure-resource access). |

Customer content submitted to AI features is processed by Azure OpenAI Service and Azure Document Intelligence within the European Economic Area (Azure regions: Sweden Central, West Europe, France Central, Germany West Central, Norway East). These services are operated by Microsoft as part of the carved-out subservice (see DC 7) and do not use customer data to train third-party models. Audio inputs are transcribed by Azure Speech Service in Sweden Central. No prompts or content are transmitted to OpenAI Inc. or Anthropic PBC directly during the examination period.

### 3.5 Third-Party Access — Production Data Path

| Vendor | Role |
|---|---|
| Microsoft Azure | Primary cloud infrastructure (sole carved-out subservice organisation). Includes Azure OpenAI Service (LLM + embeddings), Azure Document Intelligence (OCR + layout), Azure Speech Service (audio transcription), and Azure Communication Services (transactional email send). |
| Firecrawl (Mendable AI Inc.) | Web fetching, search, and content extraction for customer-supplied URL data sources. |
| BetterStack (Better Stack Inc.) | Log and trace ingestion via OpenTelemetry (data region `eu-nbg-2`, 180-day retention). |
| PostHog | Product analytics events (user, team, and organisation identifiers; event names). Collection is gated on user consent. |

Direct integrations with OpenAI Inc. and Anthropic PBC are available as deferred capabilities; neither receives customer data during the examination period. Application error tracking via Sentry is not currently deployed. Any future activation of additional subprocessors will be notified to customers under the DPA's 30-day subprocessor-change notice (DC 2).

